course: dictionary
lesson: 2381
title: Cur: an old word for a dog
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a plain meaning and an older, insulting meaning. Cur is an old word. Its first meaning is a dog of no special breed, often bad-tempered or dirty. Its second meaning is an insult used about a person.
explain: Look at the words around it. In Alice, the Mouse tells a tale about a dog called Fury, who is cruel and angry. If you read «You cur!» in an old story, someone is shouting an insult, so cur is not a kind word for a person.
explain: Ask yourself: what kind of word fits here? A name for a dog, or a name for a mean, cowardly person? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does not, try the other meaning.
explain: Old-fashioned words often make speech sound grand or angry, so the feeling matters as much as the meaning. When the context is not enough, a dictionary will give you the exact meaning.
fact: A cur is a dog of no special breed, especially one that is bad-tempered or dirty.
fact: Calling a man a cur is an old, insulting way of saying he is mean, cowardly or worthless.
fact: In Alice, a dog called Fury says, «I'll be judge, I'll be jury», in the Mouse's tale.
fact: Cur is an old word, so you will mostly meet it in older books and stories.
fact: If the sentence is about a dog, cur means a dog. If it is about a person being insulted, it means a coward or a worthless person.
exercise: «The old cur barked at every passer-by in the village.» What is a cur here? | *A bad-tempered dog | A kind teacher | A small bird | A heavy coat
exercise: «You cur!» shouted the hero at the villain. What does the insult suggest? | The villain is very tall | *The villain is mean and cowardly | The villain is a famous singer | The villain is lost in the woods
exercise: Mia reads «I'll be judge, I'll be jury» in Alice. Who says it? | *A dog called Fury | A mouse | A cook | A king
test: In an old story, «You cur!» is shouted at a man. What does cur mean here? | A tall tree | A dog of no special breed | *A mean, cowardly or worthless person | A kind friend
test: When you meet an unknown word like cur, what is the best check? | *Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Guess the longest meaning | Skip the word and never come back to it | Ask the nearest dog
exam: Read «The cur growled and snapped at the sheep.» What is a cur here, and what does it show about the dog? | *A dog of no special breed, bad-tempered and aggressive | A shepherd who is very old | A bird that sings | A sheep that is very kind
